  "details": "Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * undici: undici: Authentication bypass via cross-origin cache poisoning due to missing origin isolation (CVE-2026-85152)\n  * undici: undici: TLS certificate validation bypass in BalancedPool via dropped connect options (CVE-2026-84961)\n  * undici: undici: Denial of Service via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol (CVE-2026-19534)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * nodejs:24/nodejs: Rebase to the latest Node.js 24 release [almalinux-9.8.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-249189)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
